.TH HSH 1 "February 2026" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
hsh is a simple UNIX command language interpreter that executes commands read from the standard input.

The shell displays a prompt, reads a command line, parses it into tokens, and executes the command using fork and execve.

The shell works in both interactive and non-interactive modes.

.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.TP
.B env
Print the current environment.

.SH HOW IT WORKS
The shell performs the following steps:
1. Displays a prompt.
2. Reads input using getline.
3. Parses input into arguments.
4. Searches for the executable in PATH.
5. Creates a child process using fork.
6. Executes the command using execve.
7. Waits for the child process to terminate.

.SH RETURN VALUE
hsh returns 0 on success.

.SH AUTHORS
See AUTHORS file.

.SH BUGS
No known bugs.

.SH EXAMPLE
$ hsh
$ ls -l
$ exit
